=== 1. Operator identities ===
 dilation:  delta K = -c D K ? True
 SCT:       delta K = i S_q K ? True
 S_p in (k,mu) variables: max residual at random points = 0.e-165
 homogeneity S_q[K(lam k)] = lam (S_qK)(lam k): True

=== 2. Observer worldline, tetrad, emission surface in the tilde frame ===
 x~_o(eta) = [-eta_i**2*q1/6, -eta_i**2*q2/6, -eta_i**2*q3/6] (time independent: fluid at rest in tilde frame)
 antisymmetric Jacobian at observer (O(q) part): Matrix([[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0]])
 -> no rotation of the canonical triad at O(q); the boost part is absorbed because the triad is built orthogonal
    to the PHYSICAL fluid velocity (same worldline in both charts) -> no net aberration.

=== 3. First-order kernel K_1(k,n) (SPEC conventions, observer at origin) ===
 T_dT+T_Phi, T_v/eta at small k: eta**2*k**2/10 - 1/3 , -eta**2*k**2/30 + 1/3
 ISW integrand small-k: 0  (O(k^2))
 => local part: (T_dT+T_Phi)(1 + i k mu chi) - i k mu eta_s/3 + i k mu eta_o/3 = -1/3 + O(k^2) since chi = eta_o - eta_s;
    the constant -1/3 is removed by the monopole (and is cancelled by the observer's own [dT+Psi]_o in S_1).

